+    },
+    "2": {
+      "mascotDialogue": "Lines 4 and 5 find the biggest of the node and its two children. Line 8's recursive call is what lets that displaced value keep sinkin' past more'n one level if it's gotta."
+    },
+    "3": {
+      "mascotDialogue": "9's sittin' right up top, and every parent down this tree beats out both its kids — same array-index math as min heap, just the comparison flipped clean around."
+    },
+    "4": {
+      "mascotDialogue": "That swap alone don't finish the job. Without siftDown, you've just moved the problem up to the top of the tree instead of actually fixin' it."
+    },
